"""Root interpretation of complete saved-optimization and evidence diagnostics."""
from common_v1 import *
def fmt(v):return f"{v['mean']:+.6f} [{v['CI95'][0]:+.6f}, {v['CI95'][1]:+.6f}]"if v.get('mean')is not None else'not scorable'
def tta(ds):
 dest=P/'tta'/ds;aud=read(dest/'audit_receipt.json');assert aud['status']=='independently_verified_saved_optimizer_diagnostic_aggregates';r=read(dest/'diagnostics.json');text=f'# Actual saved Tent/SAR optimization diagnostics: {ds}\n\nComplete existing full-domain runs, {COUNTS[ds]} queries. No new model, optimizer or GT scoring. Every saved native/adapted logit and receipt SHA was checked during derivation; independent audit checks all aggregate means, principal CIs and exact update/interval counts against the original full-domain audit.\n\n|Method|Entropy before|Entropy after|Delta entropy [95% CI]|Mean saved parameter-update L2|Mean logit-change L2|Changed native intervals % [95% CI]|\n|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---|\n'
 for m,v in r['methods'].items():
  s=v['statistics'];text+=f"|{m}|{s['entropy_before']['mean']:.9f}|{s['entropy_after']['mean']:.9f}|{fmt(s['entropy_delta'])}|{s['parameter_update_L2']['mean']:.9f}|{s['logit_change_L2']['mean']:.9f}|{fmt(s['changed_native_interval_percent'])}|\n"
 text+='\n|Method|Native delta t pp [95% CI]|Native delta v pp [95% CI]|Matched joint-MAP delta t pp [95% CI]|Matched joint-MAP delta v pp [95% CI]|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n'
 for m,v in r['methods'].items():
  s=v['statistics'];text+='|'+m+'|'+'|'.join(fmt(s[k])for k in ['native_delta_t_pp','native_delta_v_pp','joint_delta_t_pp','joint_delta_v_pp'])+'|\n'
 text+='\nEntropy uses the four offset/endpoint distributions, before adaptation and saved logits from a real final forward AFTER all five updates. The last pre-update training trace is not substituted for the actual after state. Parameters are temporal-decoder LayerNorm affine only; saved state-delta L2 is the original actual trace. Source boxes stay fixed, episodic resets are exact. Centered logit changes and per-query entropy/update details are retained in all_saved_optimizer_diagnostics.tsv. SAR may have no reliable samples on some steps; original audited first/second mask counts remain authoritative.\n\nChanges to continuous distributions/parameters do not imply an argmax interval change. Tiny or null localization effects on this adapter cannot establish a universal failure of Tent/SAR, canonical BatchNorm/full-network or continual adaptation. Joint-MAP versus native readout gains must not be attributed to the optimizer: each adapter is compared to Source with the SAME readout. Current method uses eight expert observations and zero optimizer steps; these baselines use zero expert observations and five optimizer iterations. Cached decoder/adaptation runtime is not matched end-to-end deployment latency; original acquisition costs remain nonzero.\n\nQuery-equal statistics and 10000 parent-cluster pointwise95%CIs; no familywise or unseen-data claim, and no full-target retuning. All signed per-query changes and original failures/costs remain in the old and new reports.\n';(dest/'ANALYSIS.md').write_text(text);atomic(dest/'root_export_receipt.json',dict(status='root_saved_optimizer_all_signed_analysis_exported',audit_sha256=sha(dest/'audit_receipt.json'),analysis_sha256=sha(dest/'ANALYSIS.md'),code_sha256=sha(Path(__file__)),worker=identity()));print(ds,'TTA root analysis exported')
def evidence(ds):
 dest=P/'temporal_evidence'/ds;aud=read(dest/'audit_receipt.json');assert aud['status']=='independent_pairwise_AUROC_event_masks_means_CIs_verified';r=read(dest/'report.json');text=f'# Temporal evidence quality and error risk: {ds}\n\nAll {COUNTS[ds]} queries from the complete sealed/scored/cold-array-audited temporal controls. Offline GT event membership only, no action-label model or new acquisition. Independent audit rederives AUROC by explicit positive-negative pair comparisons, event masks and per-query means and CIs.\n\n|Source tIoU / diagnostic group|Queries|Scorable corrected-ROI AUROC queries|Event evidence mean|Background evidence mean|Corrected-ROI AUROC [95% CI]|Corrected-minus-Source-ROI AUROC [95% CI]|Delta t pp [95% CI]|t harm % [95% CI]|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|\n'
 for name,v in r.items():
  s=v['statistics'];text+=f"|{name}|{v['queries']}|{s.get('CorrectedROI_AUROC',{}).get('queries',0)}|{s.get('CorrectedROI_event_mean',{}).get('mean')}|{s.get('CorrectedROI_background_mean',{}).get('mean')}|{fmt(s.get('CorrectedROI_AUROC',{}))}|{fmt(s.get('Corrected_minus_Source_AUROC',{}))}|{fmt(s.get('delta_t_pp',{}))}|{fmt(s.get('harmed_t_percent',{}))}|\n"
 text+='\nSource temporal-quality bins are fixed [0,.2), [.2,.5), [.5,.8), [.8,1]. Temporal gains/harm compare current output to native untouched Source; same-joint-readout and no-expert TR controls are separately available in the temporal-control table, avoiding decoder/readout attribution. AUROC is computed WITHIN each query, with tied scores contributing one half; only queries containing both GT event and background sampled frames are scorable. Missing/one-class queries remain in outcome denominators and their counts are explicit, never assigned AUROC zero or dropped from accuracy. Event/non-event means, frame support counts and all query scores are retained. Frames are not independent bootstrap units.\n\n## Confidence and prototype separation, descriptive groups\n\n|Group|Original joint-prior peak [95% CI]|Original joint-prior entropy [95% CI]|Source-ROI prototype separation [95% CI]|Corrected-ROI prototype separation [95% CI]|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n'
 for name in ['all','temporal_improved','temporal_harmed']:
  s=r[name]['statistics'];text+='|'+name+'|'+'|'.join(fmt(s.get(k,{}))for k in ['source_joint_peak','source_joint_entropy','prototype_separation_SourceROI','prototype_separation_CorrectedROI'])+'|\n'
 text+='\nThese groups condition on the already observed offline outcome and show associations only; q0 joint-prior peak is explicitly not an independently calibrated confidence probability. Prototype separation and appearance/event discrimination are within-video self-consistency measures because evaluated frames participate in prototype fitting. A positive AUROC, object-local contrast or temporal correspondence effect does NOT establish independent action-semantics understanding or causal mutual reinforcement. No online GT gate, default selection or algorithm changes are made.\n\nA separate form x fixed-quality-thirds report separates temporal evidence at the SAME E trajectory (ExpertInitTR-FixedE_SourceTR), final spatial decoding (Ours-ExpertInitTR), and total gain (Ours-Source). Same E controlled time branches have identical frame coordinates; their vIoU difference reflects intervals, not a spatial-coordinate difference. All negative and null strata and the original interpolation comparison are retained. Pointwise parent10000 CIs, no familywise/unseen confirmation claim. Cached CPU cost is not deployment time; inherited Source/expert acquisition is nonzero.\n';(dest/'ANALYSIS.md').write_text(text);atomic(dest/'root_export_receipt.json',dict(status='root_event_evidence_and_risk_analysis_exported',audit_sha256=sha(dest/'audit_receipt.json'),analysis_sha256=sha(dest/'ANALYSIS.md'),code_sha256=sha(Path(__file__)),worker=identity()));print(ds,'evidence root analysis exported')
if __name__=='__main__':
 ap=argparse.ArgumentParser();ap.add_argument('task',choices=['tta','evidence']);ap.add_argument('--dataset',choices=COUNTS,required=True);a=ap.parse_args();globals()[a.task](a.dataset)
